vara wider project. This is a paper about what happened in selfless state from a Homo Sapie bodily self regulation perspective. So it's as I said, it's part of a wider project that consists in both theoretical and experimental components. Today we're going to look at meditation. So for people that are not really familiar with that, meditation is a practice that engaged attention to self regulate physiological and cognitive activity.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9825177788734436, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.8079928159713745, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.07965254783630371, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.05616496503353119, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.027426594868302345, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.02422962337732315, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0017079892568290234, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness'}, {'relevance': 0.001524661434814334, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}, {'relevance': 0.001266303239390254, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.00105736602563411, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 43294, 'end': 89620}, 'sentences_idx_start': 7, 'sentences_idx_end': 12}, {'text': "What we're interested here is that people that meditate with a certain experience, so for example, meditating in the past two years with regularly, like some hours per week, they consistently report losing one sense of the self or having selfless experiences. But not only that, they also report to have bodily alterations. So alterations in the procession of the body. That has been called expansion, oceanic boundlessness, dissolution of body boundaries.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8385844230651855, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.4907548427581787, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.06465158611536026, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.03051266446709633, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0253845676779747, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.004455652087926865, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.002231265651062131, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0021570001263171434, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0013834434794262052, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0013646542793139815, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 90280, 'end': 127372}, 'sentences_idx_start': 13, 'sentences_idx_end': 16}, {'text': "And since you are particularly interested in this kind of phenomenal experience, we have proposed to frame them unlimited body, just for clarity. So our question here is what exactly? And the question that will follow the whole presentation in the background is what exactly is lost when experienced meditators report losing their self and the body? So let's first look very briefly at what the self is, or the sense of self is.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8991310596466064, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.08262880146503448, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.035062387585639954, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.03092917613685131, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01762702316045761, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.006042746361345053, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.005696398206055164, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003110670018941164, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0028131839353591204, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00198019458912313, 'label': 'FineArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 127516, 'end': 160476}, 'sentences_idx_start': 17, 'sentences_idx_end': 20}, {'text': "So this concept is so complex and so wide that has been debated since the beginning of philosophy. And of course, it might be so intuitive that it's also very hard to define. But one very old and used definition is the unitary or unique individual eye. The first person perspective, that Latin was called the subjectin. So something that lay under all our stream of experience, thoughts and whatever else happens to us, that's the subject.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04512355104088783, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.041946373879909515, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.02057960443198681, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.016184335574507713, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.014630374498665333, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.00782439112663269, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EyeAndVisionConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.007042502518743277, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004364949185401201, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004004467744380236, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0034528227988630533, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 160658, 'end': 199320}, 'sentences_idx_start': 21, 'sentences_idx_end': 25}, {'text': "However, more recently in cognitive science, we are appealing to a more common definition of sense of self, a bit more exhaustive, that is defined as a multidimensional construct. And here we will come back on this concept later and we'll unpack it a bit more. So the aim of this presentation will be to first of all, lay down the fact that in self experiences, the biological organism, so to speak, the human body remains successfully repregulated.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.391183286