576556}, 'sentences_idx_start': 52, 'sentences_idx_end': 56}, {'text': "So there is something that is true consciousness or something that is the real consciousness. And this actually has broke through the concept of pure consciousness. So something that stayed there and it's purified by everything, by also the body. And there is so many definition of this pure consciousness. We brought some example like ownerless consciousness, the consciousness that doesn't have an owner, that doesn't have a self. So it doesn't have a proper sense of self that walked or that owns this consciousness.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8680654764175415, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.14404717087745667, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.032024551182985306, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.006369863171130419, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.003957831300795078, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0021380463149398565, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.00196690671145916, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.001337667228654027, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.001065017539076507, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.0009257172932848334, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 576588, 'end': 617760}, 'sentences_idx_start': 57, 'sentences_idx_end': 62}, {'text': "Mastinger has worked on the minimal phenomenal experience defining aspecial a temporal dimensional consciousness. And this is very supportive because it's consistent with the Buddhist philosophical stance of no self. So for most tradition of Buddhism, there is no self. The self, it's an illusion. And it comes to our psychology when we enter in contact with the world and with the sensations of the world and certain patterns of behavior that elicit the sense that we have a self.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.969822108745575, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.9042023420333862, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.23607702553272247, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.02790328860282898, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.01351617369800806, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.008951328694820404, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0028297388926148415, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0012360734399408102, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.001114991377107799, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0009334093774668872, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 618420, 'end': 654890}, 'sentences_idx_start': 63, 'sentences_idx_end': 67}, {'text': 'So, as I said, meditation allows us to access this pure consciousness for supporters of this thesis and rebuilds one choose an essential nature of subjective and we bring this into debate. There are also people that argue against this and it has been called by Matthew in their special issues, the Ubitiquity thesis. So the UBIT thesis claim that essential self is ubiquitous to all states of consciousness and sometimes it appeals to the immunity to error through misidentification argument of self ascription reports, which is simpler than this long name.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9946691393852234, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.6863093376159668, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.1416311264038086, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.03430384024977684, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.025427846238017082, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.012226379476487637, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.00564125319942832, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0031894040293991566, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0023760884068906307, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.002221232047304511, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 656080, 'end': 703610}, 'sentences_idx_start': 68, 'sentences_idx_end': 70}, {'text': "And it's basically the fact that I can say that I had a wonderful experience and this wonderful experience may be true or false on this weekend. I can do mistakes, I can make mistakes, but I cannot not say that I didn't have these wonderful experiences because the moment in which I report I have a perspective on this. So I cannot really be mistaking on the fact that I'm reporting this.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.05637965351343155, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>DayTrips'}, {'relevance': 0.04170086979866028, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType'}, {'relevance': 0.027831342071294785, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>FamilyTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.009671888314187527, 'label': 'Travel'}, {'relevance': 0.009458208456635475, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>BudgetTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.008276661857962608, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>BusinessTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.007463055197149515, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions'}, {'relevance': 0.0046459585428237915, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>FanConventions'}, {'relevance': 0.0032684868201613426, 'label': 'Travel>TravelType>AdventureTravel'}, {'relevance': 0.003213251009583473, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 704400, 'end': 739300}, 'sentences_idx_start': 71, 'sentences_idx_end': 73}, {'text': "Maybe I was dreaming, maybe it wasn't a wonderful experience, but it's me that I'm reporting. So the moment I'm reporting this, it means that I have to be there. And this applies also to when I ascribe myself selfless state, I had a selfless state. This is very controversial. Other problems on top of that are cross cultural problems also addressed in the literature.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1068122610449791, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.10556148737668991, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.047029122710227966, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.036245282739400864, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ContentProduction>FreelanceWriting'}, {'relevance': 0.014471037313342094, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>TravelBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.012385458685457706, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.005620521493256092, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.004440551623702049, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.003607412800192833, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>Sci-fiAndFantasy'}, {'relevance': 0.0035939218942075968, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Fiction'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 739370, 'end': 766728}, 'sentences_idx_start': 74, 'sentences_idx_end': 78}, {'text': 'So this experience selfless states may be influenced by certain vows or certain beliefs that meditator endorse, especially during especially expert meditators. And the other thing is these all cross cultural analysis and debate about the self may be also partially due to a verbal misunderstanding. So that the western philosophy may have problems about the self that actually the Eastern probably philosophy is not really addressing. So there might be some incommensurability of problems there.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9499525427818298, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.9318878054618835, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.17643845081329346, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.02300312928855419, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.004320936277508736, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.001418607891537249, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.001309778424911201, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0008259096648544073, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0005424690316431224, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.00046082393964752555, 'label': 'HealthyLiving'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 766904, 'end': 811548}, 'sentences_idx_start': 79, 'sentences_idx_end': 82}, {'text': "But as also we said in the paper, it's not that we want to address the Buddhist philosophical problems, rather we want to bring insight from these to our problems. So, given this debate, we want to propose a shift in the focus. So we don't want to start by looking at consciousness and trying to solve things about the self, but we want to start by focusing on the body. So we proposed a shift in focus in the bodily experience, examining this deep mercy state.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9890156388282776, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.89493727684021, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.057496652007102966, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0243346206843853, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0018972739344462752, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0009712395840324461, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.0007353303371928632, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0007161723333410919, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0005018641240894794, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>Biographies'}, {'relevance': 0.0004787983780261129, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 811714, 'end': 846630}, 'sentences_idx_start': 83, 'sentences_idx_end': 86}, {'text': "So let's start by the subjective experience of the body or the study of the subjective experience of the body, which is phenomenology. In the tradition, our body has a unique status. So the anatomical structure of the body has been called by USA Kobe. So the living body, the body that I can observe and others can be observed. So it's the object among the other object, they would say. But it's not only that because it's an object that I can live from inside.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9912393689155579, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.20803093910217285, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.0646820217370987, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.01993904449045658, 'label': 'FineArt>DigitalArts'}, {'relevance': 0.014435914345085621, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.007783738896250725, 'label': 'BooksAndLiterature>ArtAndPhotographyBooks'}, {'relevance': 0.007311016321182251, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.006898726802319288, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>CosmeticMedicalServices'}, {'relevance': 0.006261072587221861, 'label': 'FineArt>ModernArt'}, {'relevance': 0.005512567237019539, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 848940, 'end': 882628}, 'sentences_idx_start': 87, 'sentences_idx_end': 92}, {'text': 'So it has been called the light, the lived body or the body as I leave it from inside, as I said. So what happens to these kind of dimension? Again, we can unpack this and see how the meditative states affect them. So from the point of view of the life believed body, we already know, and I will unpack a little bit more. So we have already said that we have called unlinuated body experiences the reports that spoke about this fading of the body boundaries.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.977882981300354, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.3450416028499603, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.11197345703840256, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.023974912241101265, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.016144977882504463, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.014775130897760391, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.010149757377803326, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.008169309236109257, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.003886004677042365, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.003615927416831255, 'label': 'FineArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 882794, 'end': 921260}, 'sentences_idx_start': 93, 'sentences_idx_end': 97}, {'text': "So the body boundary has been defined as a cognitive emotional perception of one's body surface. That's just a definition. We can also debate about this. But what it's important about for us that our sense of body boundaries is flexible and dynamic. It's not fixed because we are in the realm of the body as felt from inside. There is an interesting study that exemplified this concept in relation to meditation by Jumpren in 2016, though it has worked late further on on this as well.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.9535762071609497, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.035746827721595764, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>Beauty'}, {'relevance': 0.008308812975883484, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.006851047743111849, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.004603253677487373, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.004180713091045618, 'label': "HealthyLiving>Women'sHealth"}, {'relevance': 0.003833470633253455, 'label': 'PopCulture>CelebrityPregnancy'}, {'relevance': 0.003256881609559059, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.002757854526862502, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002453945344313979, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>CosmeticMedicalServices'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 921420, 'end': 959228}, 'sentences_idx_start': 98, 'sentences_idx_end': 103}, {'text': 'But I find it interesting to look at this image because this is part of a self report measurement that they used on a sample of people that had been trained in meditation, in particular with body scanning. So that people had to systematically scan sensation running the body. And the result is that in less than four months of practice, so not actually not the expert, they really started to report an increased tendency to go towards the almost imperceptible perception of the body.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.1354127824306488, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.12399964779615402, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.10410809516906738, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0735907033085823, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.05054477974772453, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.01309996098279953, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.0053659649565815926, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.004823761992156506, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0035949174780398607, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0026326191145926714, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ConsumerElectronics>WearableTechnology'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 959394, 'end': 1001528}, 'sentences_idx_start': 104, 'sentences_idx_end': 106}, {'text': "So they conclude that meditation can be actually studied in this sense where it affects our sense of body boundaries. And they saw significant results also in relation to increased mood, happiness and decreased anxiety and rumination. But this is just another story that will come back later. So I find interesting also this quotation by Fink here in this paper it's talking about why ego dissolution may be better understood as ego expansion. And then ego dissolution comes in a later interpretation. And so I will read it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8693654537200928, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.20808589458465576, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.06891170889139175, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.026102667674422264, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.009218885563313961, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.00790345761924982, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.007756820879876614, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.007426393683999777, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.006804050877690315, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.002896079793572426, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1001694, 'end': 1053496}, 'sentences_idx_start': 107, 'sentences_idx_end': 112}, {'text': "It's not the feeling of self that dissolves, but the boundary between a feeling of self and the feeling of anything else in consciousness. So here again Pink is talking about consciousness but from our perspective this quotation is pretty informing because it goes in our direction as well because he says it's not that you're losing really yourself. This experience is dependent on how you actually perceive your boundary with you and what you don't consider you. So self fading of the self other distinction ability.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04515097290277481, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.025925440713763237, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.003889771644026041, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0027519227005541325, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0015351840993389487, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0010165689745917916, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Agnosticism'}, {'relevance': 0.0009828569600358605, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0007040301570668817, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.000699306488968432, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.00044567041913978755, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1053598, 'end': 1094120}, 'sentences_idx_start': 113, 'sentences_idx_end': 116}, {'text': 'So here it comes predictive processing acting framework because we want to basically breach this phenomenal subjective experience to cognitive phenomena and underlying mechanistic explanation. Indeed, predictive processing activities have recently used for this purpose. Also meditation research and psychopathology research and so on. So in this presentation I will use them in an interchangeable way but following certain trends.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7835293412208557, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.49300798773765564, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.04390832036733627, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.022232703864574432, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.019246743991971016, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.010539688169956207, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.005374532658606768, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0044340891763567924, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Astrology'}, {'relevance': 0.00378854270093143, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.003745310241356492, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1096380, 'end': 1137552}, 'sentences_idx_start': 117, 'sentences_idx_end': 120}, {'text': "But it doesn't have to be, it's also under debate and I will also give API purely I don't know how to say theoretical perspective on that I will not go too much technical. So briefly, this framework considers brains as predictive machine or as Friesen likes to say, consider brain as a fantastic organ which is because it's not only able to do amazing things, but also because it really generates fantasies about the world.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.999255359172821, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.08121628314256668, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.06591008603572845, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.00389371276833117, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.002259328030049801, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>InternetOfThings'}, {'relevance': 0.0021918858401477337, 'label': 'BusinessAndFinance>Business>BusinessI.T.'}, {'relevance': 0.0010640869149938226, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0010426095686852932, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0007759705185890198, 'label': 'Automotive>AutoType>DriverlessCars'}, {'relevance': 0.0005993196391500533, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>Internet>ITAndInternetSupport'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 1137616, 'end': 1179164}, 'sentences_idx_start': 121, 'sentences_idx_end': 122}, {'text': 'And this is because in order to act, interact with itself and the world around, the brain constantly anticipate the current state of affairs in order to make sense of the sensorium or the stream of experiences that happens. So it possess or embody or utilizes, it depends on the commitment a generative model which is a model that keep tracks of regularity of the world and forms predictions out of it in a hie