vance': 0.0017946697771549225, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3175704, 'end': 3207990}, 'sentences_idx_start': 307, 'sentences_idx_end': 312}, {'text': "I think the first one because it's just for me personally, I'm curious about that is that those deep meditative selfless states I think that can also be reached while doing yoga, right? Basically the opposite of sitting still. It's like a sort of repetitive movement actually. So I'm wondering do those movements have to be perfectly predictable in order to be attenuated and then reaching the same state? Or is that like a different different concept or how do you put that in your framework?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.32207199931144714, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.024979645386338234, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.009343797340989113, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.009336498565971851, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005065332632511854, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0023676033597439528, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.0010602393886074424, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Religious(MusicAndAudio)'}, {'relevance': 0.0005240997998043895, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0005059660761617124, 'label': 'FineArt>Dance'}, {'relevance': 0.00044239824637770653, 'label': 'Sports>MartialArts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3209080, 'end': 3240160}, 'sentences_idx_start': 313, 'sentences_idx_end': 317}, {'text': "I think here you brought mainly two topics. One is, is it possible to reach deep matter states also not sitting in a still position? And the answer is yes. However, there is not so much research on that. So I can talk about anecdotal knowledge, but I did not read so much about walking meditation effect, usually walking meditation or of course you talk about yoga. I know, but that's what I would say, that walking meditation is used as a complementary practice through the sitting.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.26079022884368896, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0778907909989357, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.05685059353709221, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.032896820455789566, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.023059774190187454, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.002045045606791973, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0016074475133791566, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.000839106913190335, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0006008712807670236, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.0005253874696791172, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3244500, 'end': 3291520}, 'sentences_idx_start': 318, 'sentences_idx_end': 323}, {'text': "So I would say it's hard to reach deep meditative states only by walking meditation. In regarding to yoga, also yoga means unity. So what we think about yoga now, we think about movement, but it's always accompanied by reaching state of concentration through meditation. So you cannot have yoga without meditation, otherwise you'll be stretching or pilates. But second topic is that can it happen when you don't have prediction of movement? Right?", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5275802612304688, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.014090165495872498, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.011239520274102688, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.005781249143183231, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.005122489761561155, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.002354410709813237, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.001577485236339271, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0011685959761962295, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Religious(MusicAndAudio)'}, {'relevance': 0.001135453232564032, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.0006211950676515698, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3292260, 'end': 3338096}, 'sentences_idx_start': 324, 'sentences_idx_end': 329}, {'text': "No, I meant like because in yoga at least I don't really do yoga, right? But I can imagine that when people reach those states doing yoga, then they kind of do it almost like in a trance type of way. They're always doing the same movement over and over and over again so that they don't have to attend to those movements. But it's just like an automatic process. I was wondering if that also can I jump in? Actually, this is precisely the opposite.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.06497969478368759, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.032085902988910675, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.01635524071753025, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.003026999067515135, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.002895801793783903, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.0018324387492612004, 'label': 'FineArt>Dance'}, {'relevance': 0.0018246581312268972, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0006114795687608421, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Religious(MusicAndAudio)'}, {'relevance': 0.0006064348272047937, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0005878707161173224, 'label': 'Sports>MartialArts'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3338278, 'end': 3364200}, 'sentences_idx_start': 330, 'sentences_idx_end': 335}, {'text': "What Valerie was saying is so Valerie was saying this is precisely the opposite. You want to reach through yoga just like the opposite of automatic. So basically when you do this movements, you need to be united with yourself doing it. So you really need to I'm doing yoga so the past ten years and precisely this is like they're trying to tell us don't do it on automatic. Because it's like when you have your thinking happening there and your body is doing some stuff there, right.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.04343309625983238, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.012801463715732098, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.005205768626183271, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>PhysicalTherapy'}, {'relevance': 0.004731208551675081, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0020472712349146605, 'label': 'Sports>MartialArts'}, {'relevance': 0.001785610569640994, 'label': 'FineArt>Dance'}, {'relevance': 0.0010589336743578315, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006664529792033136, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>FitnessAndExercise'}, {'relevance': 0.0006172062712721527, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0003795410448219627, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Religious(MusicAndAudio)'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3364620, 'end': 3399652}, 'sentences_idx_start': 336, 'sentences_idx_end': 340}, {'text': "You need to basically be presence in every single type of moon. So you have like fully, fully presence if you do it automatically, that's more like gymnastic or something. But it's interesting. So your point is really interesting because then would be really nice to have a control condition where we have people doing like movement, meditation and yoga and then contrast with the phenomena of some other sense retenuation and whether they have what type of embodiment and disembodiment and gentivity experiences they have.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.684917151927948, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.14012408256530762, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.08179876208305359, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.06754333525896072, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.0374055877327919, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00849990639835596, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.008274261839687824, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.004349502269178629, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.00403442420065403, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.003373111132532358, 'label': 'FineArt>Dance'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 3399786, 'end': 3433950}, 'sentences_idx_start': 341, 'sentences_idx_end': 344}, {'text': "Okay, I don't know exactly what I was trying to get it. But I think it was also more related to because you said that when meditating you have to sort of let yourself letting go. Letting go, exactly. And the idea is that everything has to be perfectly sort of predictable, right? That's the idea behind it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.25767582654953003, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.04268954321742058, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.0006651841104030609, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0006207351689226925, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0005493233911693096, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0005058440729044378, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.00035086198477074504, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.00017893170297611505, 'label': 'FamilyAndRelationships>Bereavement'}, {'relevance': 0.00015699132927693427, 'label': 'Education>Ea