 show. So that's super nice.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.01725766807794571, 'label': 'EventsAndAttractions>PersonalCelebrations&LifeEvents>Birth'}, {'relevance': 0.00522620277479291, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.005128188990056515, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BoneAndJointConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.004669045563787222, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>Surgery'}, {'relevance': 0.003929396625608206, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>CosmeticMedicalServices'}, {'relevance': 0.003430061973631382, 'label': 'Science>BiologicalSciences'}, {'relevance': 0.00280808936804533, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>MedicalTests'}, {'relevance': 0.0024755122140049934, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>Ear,NoseAndThroatConditions'}, {'relevance': 0.0015428242040798068, 'label': 'Science'}, {'relevance': 0.0014254921115934849, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>EndocrineAndMetabolicDiseases>HormonalDisorders'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4967558, 'end': 4996090}, 'sentences_idx_start': 548, 'sentences_idx_end': 557}, {'text': "And then the next steps would be to create or develop computational model around this, basically contrast the real world data with, you know, simulation data and then have a multilayered type of approach with different methods, from physiological to behavioral to phenomenological to computational, potentially also neural. So that's something would be nice to do in the next steps. And apart from that, I think that's all for now, and I'll leave the floor to Valeria.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8727500438690186, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>ArtificialIntelligence'}, {'relevance': 0.09253642708063126, 'label': 'VideoGaming>VideoGameGenres>SimulationVideoGames'}, {'relevance': 0.042079344391822815, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.022482573986053467, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>VirtualReality'}, {'relevance': 0.008936121128499508, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Robotics'}, {'relevance': 0.00769867654889822, 'label': 'Technology&Computing'}, {'relevance': 0.0060334219597280025, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>AugmentedReality'}, {'relevance': 0.004095206502825022, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>BrainAndNervousSystemDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.003500677878037095, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ProgrammingLanguages'}, {'relevance': 0.0025778186973184347, 'label': 'Technology&Computing>Computing>ComputerSoftwareAndApplications>3-DGraphics'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 4996780, 'end': 5044280}, 'sentences_idx_start': 558, 'sentences_idx_end': 560}, {'text': "Well, again, thank you, Dan and everybody. Yeah. I also want to thank you a lot for this platform, this invitation. It was really nice. Really nice person and really nice conversation. I'm working with Anne Andy's project, so she already said, what's the next direction? What. I can add in this I think would be on the theoretical side also start engaging with more closely to bodily reactions to meditation because the body boundaries dissolution is just one part of it.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.5865073204040527, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.24370010197162628, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.02536064200103283, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.012241482734680176, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.012179620563983917, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.0028259216342121363, 'label': 'Style&Fashion>BodyArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0013613863848149776, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.0009636714239604771, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>MentalHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.0008878692169673741, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0008016836363822222, 'label': 'FineArt'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5045740, 'end': 5086708}, 'sentences_idx_start': 561, 'sentences_idx_end': 568}, {'text': "It's like one part of the phenomenology but it's not the only thing that happens during meditation. There is a lot of potential that can be discovered on this because the body boundary solution again, it's really study a lot, but it's a phenomenon and there is so many other things that happens in our body while we meditate and I speak for first person experience, but in the community it's really like already said, other kinds of also more healing traditions like breath work, for example.", 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.7189245820045471, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.6267850399017334, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Buddhism'}, {'relevance': 0.06444689631462097, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine>HolisticHealth'}, {'relevance': 0.041742537170648575, 'label': 'HealthyLiving>Wellness>AlternativeMedicine'}, {'relevance': 0.02088400535285473, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality'}, {'relevance': 0.008525148034095764, 'label': 'Religion&Spirituality>Hinduism'}, {'relevance': 0.001354256528429687, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'relevance': 0.0007889324333518744, 'label': 'MedicalHealth>DiseasesAndConditions>SleepDisorders'}, {'relevance': 0.0005877417861483991, 'label': 'FineArt'}, {'relevance': 0.0005238837911747396, 'label': 'MusicAndAudio>Religious(MusicAndAudio)'}], 'timestamp': {'start': 5086794, 'end': 5122610}, 'sentences_idx_start': 569, 'sentences_idx_end': 570}, {'text': 'There there is a lot of potential where people already work on that. But there is no bridge with the academic communities. So people work pragmatically with this intuitive knowledge about what happens in the body during these altered states of consciousness but still we need to bridge it with trying to make sense from a phonological and scientific point of view and experimental point of view as well.', 'labels': [{'relevance': 0.8732936382293701, 'label': 'Hobbies&Interests>ParanormalPhenomena'}, {'releva