fidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'on', 'start': 2885178, 'end': 2885364, 'confidence': 0.99993, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'it.', 'start': 2885402, 'end': 2885990, 'confidence': 0.99805, 'speaker': 'B'}]}, {'text': "Is it my turn? Sure. Did I miss? Yeah. So obviously I don't have many questions because it's like we wrote this together.", 'start': 2890020, 'end': 2900790, 'confidence': 0.79779, 'words': [{'text': 'Is', 'start': 2890020, 'end': 2890384, 'confidence': 0.79779, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'it', 'start': 2890422, 'end': 2890576, 'confidence': 0.99999, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'my', 'start': 2890598, 'end': 2890784, 'confidence': 0.99986, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'turn?', 'start': 2890822, 'end': 2891360, 'confidence': 0.97598, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'Sure.', 'start': 2891510, 'end': 2891872, 'confidence': 0.99287, 'speaker': 'B'}, {'text': 'Did', 'start': 2891926, 'end': 2892096, 'confidence': 0.95009, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'I', 'start': 2892118, 'end': 2892208, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'miss?', 'start': 2892214, 'end': 2892720, 'confidence': 0.72, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'Yeah.', 'start': 2892870, 'end': 2893570, 'confidence': 0.8168, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'So', 'start': 2895380, 'end': 2895984, 'confidence': 0.96346, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'obviously', 'start': 2896102, 'end': 2896432, 'confidence': 0.99994, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'I', 'start': 2896486, 'end': 2896656, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': "don't", 'start': 2896678, 'end': 2896780, 'confidence': 0.99884, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'have', 'start': 2896790, 'end': 2896964, 'confidence': 0.99805, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'many', 'start': 2897002, 'end': 2897204, 'confidence': 0.9998, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'questions', 'start': 2897242, 'end': 2897540, 'confidence': 0.99996, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'because', 'start': 2897610, 'end': 2897892, 'confidence': 0.99993, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': "it's", 'start': 2897946, 'end': 2898128, 'confidence': 0.99727, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'like', 'start': 2898144, 'end': 2898372, 'confidence': 0.99983, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'we', 'start': 2898426, 'end': 2899030, 'confidence': 0.99981, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'wrote', 'start': 2899400, 'end': 2899904, 'confidence': 0.83223, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'this', 'start': 2899952, 'end': 2900164, 'confidence': 0.99998, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'together.', 'start': 2900202, 'end': 2900790, 'confidence': 0.97613, 'speaker': 'C'}]}, {'text': "But I think what I would like just to add not really a question is I really like to see so for instance like in ideal world would be nice to get all the traditions of the meditative experiences and how they relate to the body and make a very precise prediction on what exactly they will kind of predict in terms of certain sensory experiences and how this can be interpreted through different theoretical lenses. I think that could be really interesting because I think one of the problems, the challenges that we have right now is that we have so many concepts, so many approaches and kind of, like, scattered all over the map, and I think would be really nice to narrow down, because, as you said, Daniel so everybody knows what meditation is. Everybody knows at least one person that meditates in life and everything, but it's really unclear what exactly we are after and why. In certain cases, this is kind of like beneficial, and in other cases, basically it has negative consequences. And this is why precisely we are doing this project on depersonalization and meditation.", 'start': 2902680, 'end': 2998960, 'confidence': 0.99695, 'words': [{'text': 'But', 'start': 2902680, 'end': 2903430, 'confidence': 0.99695, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'I', 'start': 2904520, 'end': 2904884, 'confidence': 1.0, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'think', 'start': 2904922, 'end': 2905604, 'confidence': 0.99997, 'speaker': 'C'}, {'text': 'what', 'start': 2905802, 'end': 2906116, 'confidence': 0.9